# SquirrelJME GenAI Coding Guidelines and Agents Policy

GenAI is not permitted for this project due to legal concerns.
SquirrelJME is not a general 95% project it is an extremely
specialized project with specialized needs, GenAI as it exists now is not in
any way useful for SquirrelJME. GenAI cannot currently understand the context
of what SquirrelJME is and what it is for.

For those who feel that GenAI allows them to do something that they would never
otherwise do, this is something that we call _Imposter Syndrome_. You can do
things, it takes time to learn however the learning process, although it can
at times be frustrating it can be very fulfilling. It is understood that such
tools can be used to assist with the learning process, however do remember
to verify all sources and to take the output with a grain of salt. Do not give
up.

This policy only applies to Large Language Models (LLMs) and "Chatbots" which
take human language and/or expression as input to generate an output that
is not used for the purposes of accessibility.

This policy does not apply to "Traditional" AI such as neural networks,
video game "computer" players, and similar technologies. This policy does not
apply to single line code completion, search suggestions, or other basic
"smart" IDE features such as Search Anywhere, Run Anything, Tab Completion, and
IntelliSense.

This policy does not apply to dependencies, this is solely for SquirrelJME, it
is not possible to affect the policy of dependencies in any way.

## Contributing to SquirrelJME

Note that SquirrelJME does not accept any contributions from which GenAI has
been used in any fashion. It is not possible to determine the original
licensing and copyright of the generated source code, nor with information
it has assisted with due to patents. GenAI models have been trained upon
various projects with different code guidelines and licenses.
As such, the output of the GenAI cannot ultimately be currently verified.

## Future Policy Reservation

Note that at this current time, use for or against GenAI is being discussed
heavily by individuals and organizations. This policy has zero intention to
make any kind of statement in the manner, nor to judge users for evaluating
a tool for their own needs. Additionally, it is not possible in any way for
the project to prevent usage of GenAI proliferation. It is not possible to
prevent the project from being used by GenAI tools short of closing the source.
The project itself has no desire to close the source code to prevent its use
in GenAI tools. This project will not take any efforts to sabotage and/or
poison itself to make any kind of statement as this causes harm and erodes 
trust. This will project will additionally not offer any suggestions, 
encouragement, opportunity, or pledges to promote sabotage and/or poisoning. 
Specific vocabulary and wording has been intentionally avoided in this 
reservation. This reservation neither condones nor disregards future use of 
GenAI.

Permitted use of GenAI with SquirrelJME with only authorized tools may be 
accepted in the future, if all the following conditions are met:

 * The GenAI models are solely trained on SquirrelJME's source code, notes,
   history, and documentation.
 * No generic models or additional models are applied, this includes additional
   models which provide support for human languages.
 * It must not train from any other source that is not SquirrelJME.
 * The use of the GenAI is run on the local device whether that be a CPU,
   GPU, or NPU without the use of an internet and network connection, it
   must be fully usable offline.
 * The models must be fully reproducible and deterministic, the same input
   must result in the same output.
 * The models must be able to be trained fully offline on the local device.
 * The model training, prompt, and all other related software must be under an
   Open Source Initiative (OSI) license.
 * The tool has been vetted and approved by the administrators of SquirrelJME.

